# Crustum BlazeCast

Prefer package docs and the `blazecast-development` skill for orientation.

@scoped(['config/blazecast.php', 'config/bootstrap.php'])
## BlazeCast server config
- Keep app `id` / `key` / `secret` aligned with Broadcasting and Echo/Pusher client env.
- When server `path` is set (e.g. `/ws`), use the same prefix on Broadcasting `options.path` and Echo `wsPath`.
- Restrict `allowed_origins` carefully — non-matching `Origin` is rejected.
- Load `config/blazecast.php` from bootstrap after manifest install.
@endscoped

@scoped(['config/broadcasting.php'])
## Broadcasting ↔ BlazeCast
- Use Pusher driver credentials matching BlazeCast applications.
- Align `options.host` / `port` / `scheme` / `path` / TLS with the running `blazecast server`.
@endscoped

@scoped(['webroot/js/**', 'resources/**/*.js', 'assets/**/*.js'])
## Echo client (BlazeCast)
- Match key / wsHost / port / wsPath / TLS to BlazeCast and Broadcasting options.
- Auth endpoint remains Broadcasting `/broadcasting/auth` for private/presence.
@endscoped
